{
 "_comment": "Closes the open shell edge tools/repairs/duck-underfloor.json left along the bottom of Duck's plow. Cutting the panel off at the tyre line opens the scan shell: from in front of the machine, at floor level, you looked into the inside of the plow down its whole 3.5ft width. Two plates, not one — the plow has a RAISED CENTRE over the beak (measured: no geometry at all below y=0.03 between game x -0.76 and +0.43, exactly as the reference photo shows) and a plate spanning that gap would hang in mid air under the duck's head. Each outline traces the shell's own measured cross-section per 0.035ft column, pulled 0.004ft INSIDE it so the plate's walls never land coplanar with the shell's and z-fight. Extruded across game y 0.002..0.026, which brackets the jagged cut rim (its vertices land between y 0.004 and 0.020 because glb-carve tests triangle CENTROIDS). Colour is not a guess: it is the median base-colour texel under the 8107 plow triangles below y=0.10, sRGB 184,180,170, converted to the LINEAR baseColorFactor below; metallic/roughness copied off Material_tripo_part_6.",
